title RecruitBook Batch 6 — Admissions Shortlists Domain Subset

left to right direction

' Reused object (Batch 5 — unchanged this batch)
class AdmissionsOfficerProfile <<trust>> {
  id : uuid
  application_user_id : uuid
  ' verified-officer identity (Batch 5); unchanged this batch
}

' Reused object (Batch 2 — unchanged this batch)
class StudentProfile <<sensitive>> {
  id : uuid
  application_user_id : uuid
  ' Batch 2 content columns unchanged.
  ' NO shortlist-related column of any kind here.
}

' New Batch 6 object — the single prototype table
class ShortlistEntry <<value-object>> {
  id : uuid
  admissions_officer_application_user_id : uuid
  student_profile_id : uuid
  created_at : timestamptz
  ' server-derived owner id at insert (never client-supplied)
  ' UNIQUE (officer, profile); NO other columns
}

class RowLevelSecurityPolicy <<policy>> {
  current_application_user_id() : uuid
  is_verified_admissions_officer() : boolean
  is_admissions_visible_profile(profile_id) : boolean
  ' current_application_user_id() reused unchanged (Batch 1/2)
}

AdmissionsOfficerProfile "1" *-- "0..*" ShortlistEntry : owns (Batch 6 — direct,\nno Shortlist container;\nmatched on application_user_id)
ShortlistEntry "0..*" --> "1" StudentProfile : references (lookup key only)
RowLevelSecurityPolicy ..> ShortlistEntry : ownership gate — current_application_user_id()\n= admissions_officer_application_user_id\n(SELECT, INSERT via RLS; removal via a\nSECURITY DEFINER RPC, not a DELETE policy)
RowLevelSecurityPolicy ..> StudentProfile : is_admissions_visible_profile(\nstudent_profile_id) at query time
RowLevelSecurityPolicy ..> AdmissionsOfficerProfile : is_verified_admissions_officer()\nreads role/status

note right of ShortlistEntry
  Batch 6 refinement: this IS the catalog
  ShortlistEntry object, refined into the
  future table admissions_shortlist_entries.
  There is no separate "AdmissionsShortlistEntry"
  class — same catalog name, one new table.
  Bare reference only: no student content is
  denormalized onto this row (no preferred name,
  no country, no major, etc.). Every read renders
  live StudentProfile summary data through the
  existing visibility gate, never a cached copy.
end note

note bottom of RowLevelSecurityPolicy
  Three distinct gates, re-evaluated at QUERY TIME
  (not "both helpers" — ownership is now its own
  named gate alongside the two Batch 5 helpers):
  * current_application_user_id() — ownership gate
    (admissions_officer_application_user_id = self):
    required on SELECT and INSERT (RLS), and
    re-implemented directly inside the removal
    RPC's own WHERE clause (DELETE is NOT an RLS
    policy — see the amendment note below).
  * is_verified_admissions_officer() — required on
    INSERT (RLS) and inside the removal RPC
    (not on SELECT).
  * is_admissions_visible_profile(profile_id) —
    required on SELECT and INSERT; removal is
    deliberately NOT visibility-gated, so a stale
    entry can still be removed.
  A stale, withdrawn, or suspended-owner profile
  disappears from SELECT immediately — no cached
  or derived visibility field, no updated_at, and
  no update trigger for this table.
  --
  AMENDMENT (post-Group-1a): there is no direct
  DELETE RLS policy. Postgres implicitly ANDs a
  table's SELECT policies into DELETE row-
  targeting, so a visibility-gated SELECT policy
  would silently veto any DELETE policy before its
  own USING clause is consulted — a stale entry
  could never actually be reached. Removal instead
  goes exclusively through a hardened SECURITY
  DEFINER function, remove_own_admissions_
  shortlist_entry(entry_id), which bypasses RLS
  internally and re-implements ownership +
  verified-officer authorization itself. DELETE
  privilege is revoked from authenticated, making
  the RPC the provably sole removal path.
end note

note as N_Ratification
  This is a Group 1a PROPOSED shape only,
  not implemented schema. It requires the
  mandatory pre-migration design
  review at Group 2 before any migration
  is written.
end note

note as N_Excluded
  Deliberately NOT modeled:
  * Shortlist object/table — no named or
    multiple shortlists per officer
  * Entry notes, labels, or tags
  * updated_at / any update trigger or path
  * Direct officer/entry access to
    ProfileVisibilitySettings — mediated
    ONLY by is_admissions_visible_profile(...)
  * Student or Counselor access of any kind
  * Search, filters, ranking, messaging,
    notifications, exports, AI, uploads,
    audit events
end note

@enduml
